From 3afdeac2d9ad8416bbbb131b5d19e5aebca053fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mphuongth <mphuongth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 15:15:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(brand): swap donut for stacked-stones logo (cairn
 metaphor)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The donut was the right mark for "Allocate" — it pictured budget
allocation literally as a pie. For "Cairn" it's a metaphor mismatch:
a cairn is a *stack of stones* marking a trail, not a radial chart.
This replaces the mark with a stacked-stones silhouette that actually
reinforces the name.

Same navy + emerald palette, same file names and sizes, so no other
code needs to change. Browser tab favicons, PWA icons, apple-touch
icons, and wordmarks all swap to the new mark automatically.

Design decisions:
- Four stones (bottom → top), decreasing width, with small alternating
  horizontal offsets (±8px) for the hand-balanced feel of a real trail
  cairn rather than a rigid column
- Emerald on the third stone preserves the brand pop at every size
- Cream peak reads as a summit marker on the icon (navy bg); wordmarks
  swap that peak to navy when the wordmark is used on a light surface
- Stone corner radius ≈ 42% of stone height — rounded-rectangle
  boulders, not ovals, not slabs

Parameterized the same way the donut was: a STONES array at the top
of `scripts/generate-icons.mjs` holds width/height/offset/color per
stone, all as ratios of the canvas size, so the glyph scales crisply
from 32 → 1024 and rebalancing the silhouette is a single-array edit.

- scripts/generate-icons.mjs: rewritten around the STONES config
- public/icon-{192,512}.png, apple-touch-icon.png, favicon-32.png:
  regenerated from the new script
- public/cairn-icon.svg, cairn-icon-transparent.svg: regenerated
- public/cairn-wordmark.svg, cairn-wordmark-dark.svg: rebuilt with
  the stones glyph replacing the donut glyph

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
